      "label": "Multi-step moving estimate form — design brief item 20, distinct from the existing single-step 05-quote-form.json (that one stays; the brief's own five primary conversion actions name both “Request a free quote” and “Calculate a starting moving estimate” as separate actions). Built as ONE real Bricks form element (all fields for all 8 steps live in a single <form>, one submission, one email) with step PANELS shown/hidden via _interactions on the Next/Back buttons — not a native Bricks “wizard mode”, because Bricks 2.3.6's form element has no such mode (verified against includes/elements/form.php). \n\nHONEST LIMITATION, read before shipping: hiding a required field with _display:none removes it from native HTML5 validation in most browsers, so nothing here stops a visitor from clicking through to the last step without filling earlier required fields — there is no documented Bricks interaction for “validate step, then advance.” Two real fixes, neither attempted here: (a) custom JS on each Next button's click interaction (the `javascript` action type exists for this) that checks the current step's required fields before calling show/hide, or (b) rebuild this as a WS Form multi-step form — WS Form is the project's actual confirmed forms plugin (Crown_Movers_Content_Architecture_Spec_v2.md §9) and has real native multi-step support, which this Bricks-native version does not. Treat what's built here as a solid, reusable field list / content / visual design, not a production-ready validated wizard. \n\nNo pricing calculator: per spec §9, “the instant quote calculator remains a separate workstream. No pricing logic is reverse-engineered or inferred; formulas come from Crown Movers in writing.” The final step is an honest ‘request received’ confirmation, matching 05-quote-form.json's existing successMessage pattern — never a fabricated number. \n\nRadio-card visual: options below use Bricks' native `radio` field type (real inputs, real required validation) rather than a hand-styled card look, because Bricks' documented form field-styling keys (fieldBorder/fieldPadding/fieldBackgroundColor/fieldTypography) apply uniformly to the whole form, not per-option — achieving the design brief's bordered-card-per-option look with a selected-state fill needs either confirmed Bricks 2.3.6 radio markup selectors (verify once pasted into a live builder) or a small custom element. Functionally correct either way; only the visual polish is deferred."
    },
